  "body": {
    "id": "prop:fixed-gap-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "Uniformly over any collection of sequences for which\n\\[\n \\max_{k\\in\\mathcal K_n}|\\widehat C_{n,k}/n-\\mathfrak r_{n,k}|=o_{\\mathbb P_n}(1),\n \\qquad\n \\max_{k\\in\\mathcal K_n}\\left|\\sqrt n\\{\\widehat\\tau_{n,k}-\\tau_n-b_{n,k}\\}-G_{n,k}\\right|=o_{\\mathbb P_n}(1),\n\\]\nif the unique prefix \\(k_n^{\\star}\\) satisfies\n\\(\\min_{l\\ne k_n^{\\star}}\\{\\mathfrak r_{n,l}-\\mathfrak r_{n,k_n^{\\star}}\\}\\geq\\varepsilon\\), then \\(\\mathbb P_n(\\widehat k_n=k_n^{\\star})\\to1\\), and the bounded-Lipschitz distance between the law of \\(\\sqrt n(\\widehat\\tau_{n,\\widehat k_n}-\\tau_n-b_{n,k_n^{\\star}})\\) and \\(N(0,\\Gamma_n(k_n^{\\star},k_n^{\\star}))\\) tends to zero.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(\\mathbf P\\)",
      "\\(k\\)",
      "\\(l\\)",
      "\\(k_n^{\\star}\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak r_{n,k}\\)",
      "\\(P_n\\)",
      "\\(\\mathbb P_n\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat k_n\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat C_{n,k}\\)",
      "\\(G_n\\)",
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat\\tau_{n,k}\\)",
      "\\(\\tau_n\\)",
      "\\(b_{n,k}\\)",
      "\\(\\Gamma_n\\)",
      "\\(\\varepsilon\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:global-regular-law-class",
      "def:local-coordinates",
      "def:yang-prefix-estimators"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Let\n\\[\n E_n=\\left\\{\\max_k|\\widehat C_{n,k}/n-\\mathfrak r_{n,k}|<\\varepsilon/3\\right\\}.\n\\]\nThe first assumed approximation gives \\(\\inf_{\\mathbf P}\\mathbb P_n(E_n)\\to1\\).  On \\(E_n\\), every \\(l\\ne k_n^{\\star}\\) satisfies\n\\[\n \\frac{\\widehat C_{n,l}-\\widehat C_{n,k_n^{\\star}}}{n}\n \\geq \\mathfrak r_{n,l}-\\mathfrak r_{n,k_n^{\\star}}-2\\varepsilon/3\n \\geq\\varepsilon/3>0.\n\\]\nHence \\(\\widehat k_n=k_n^{\\star}\\) on \\(E_n\\), proving uniform selection consistency.  On that event the selected centered statistic equals the oracle centered statistic.  The second assumed approximation gives\n\\[\n \\sqrt n(\\widehat\\tau_{n,k_n^{\\star}}-\\tau_n-b_{n,k_n^{\\star}})\n =G_{n,k_n^{\\star}}+o_P(1).\n\\]\nBecause \\(G_{n,k_n^{\\star}}\\sim N(0,\\Gamma_n(k_n^{\\star},k_n^{\\star}))\\), the same bounded-Lipschitz argument used in the quadratic transfer proof establishes the asserted Gaussian approximation.  Replacing the oracle coordinate by the selected coordinate changes expectations of bounded test functions by at most \\(2\\mathbb P_n(E_n^c)=o(1)\\).",
